# Rocdown language reference

Rocdown is Markdown with explicit document-root declarations. Ordinary prose,
email addresses, handles, and fenced code retain their Markdown meaning.

## Declaration recognition

A reserved declaration is recognized only when it starts at the document root,
after optional indentation, and its header matches the expected shape. Reserved
names inside lists, block quotes, or fences stay Markdown.

Use `\@roc` for a literal line-start declaration example outside a fence.

## Declarations

| Form | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `@page { ... }` | Route, draft, layout, theme, color scheme, and metadata |
| `@roc { ... }` | Roc imports, types, values, and helpers |
| `@render { expr }` | Insert one Roc `Html` expression |
| `@component` | Declare a Rocci component |
| `@fixture` | Tag preview or test data |
| `@css { ... }` | Add file-scoped CSS |
| `@context`, `@init`, `@on` | Declare a standalone server app |
| `@if`, `@for`, `@match`, `@let` | Insert document-root Rocci template regions |
| `@use "./Module.rocci"` | Interactive only: import `@component` exports as `:kind` article blocks |
| `<Tag />` | Instantiate a document-root Rocci component or element |
| `:kind[params]` | Article block; see below |
| `:img[src: "...", alt: "..."]` | Native image element; `alt` or `decorative` required; see below |

`@island` is reserved in the design but not parsed yet. Hybrid sites use
`@component` hosts and `@on` handlers instead.

`@roc` is the place for Roc values and helpers. Live pages may `import pf.Sqlite`
there and call those helpers from `@on` / `@init`. Document-root text that looks
like Roc is Markdown, not a module item.

## `:img` native images

Use `:img[...]` for first-class image elements with compile-time field extraction and optional sizing. Meaningful images require `alt`. Set `decorative: Bool.true` for purely decorative images (`alt=""`). A non-empty `alt` together with `decorative: Bool.true` is an error. Markdown `![](path)` remains the empty-alt decorative shorthand. A paragraph that is only a Markdown image, and ATX headings, parse as the same internal `img` / `h1`–`h6` blocks as `:img` and `:h2`. Explicit `:h2[id: "install"]` keeps that id in the outline.

Local `src` paths, including `./img/photo.png`, resolve against the source file
directory. Site-root paths like `/assets/photo.png` and remote `http(s):` /
`data:` URLs pass through. Missing local files are errors in `rocdown run` and in
Rocdown catalog checks. Standalone preview copies those files without hashing and
serves them beside the page route; static site builds hash files under `build.assets`.

````rocdown
:img[src: "./img/yammi_banana.png", alt: "A delicious banana", width: "50px", loading: "lazy", decoding: "async"]
````

| Field | Requirement | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `src` | **Required** | Compile-time string literal path or URL |
| `alt` | Required unless `decorative` | Accessible description |
| `decorative` | Optional | `Bool.true` emits empty `alt` for purely decorative images |
| `title` | Optional | Tooltip text |
| `width` | Optional | Explicit width string (e.g. `"50px"`, `"100%"`) |
| `height` | Optional | Explicit height string (e.g. `"50px"`, `"auto"`) |
| `class` | Optional | Custom class name appended to `.rd-image` |
| `loading` | Optional | `"lazy"` or `"eager"` |
| `decoding` | Optional | `"async"`, `"auto"`, or `"sync"` |

## Article blocks

Article blocks use `:kind` at document root. Params are in `[]`. Content is
the rest of the line, a `{{ }}` section, or `:kind.begin` ... `:kind.end`.
Do not mix `.begin` with double braces on the same call. Kinds such
as `note` or `tabs` are registry names, not reserved `@` names. Line-start
`@docs` / `@img` is a removal error. Rocdown types the body; standalone
`rocdown run` paints a conservative preview.

````rocdown
:note[title: "Deprecation"] {{
    This API will be removed in 0.4. See [Routing](/docs/reference/rocdown-site/).
}}

:tabs.begin[group: "install", kind: "tool"]
    :tab[id: "cli", label: "CLI"] Check the catalog.
    :tab[id: "test", label: "Examples"] Run declared examples.
:tabs.end
````

Nested article blocks are legal in the body unless the parent kind's child
policy forbids them. `:tabs` accepts only `:tab` children (Markdown and other
blocks are errors). `:card-grid` accepts only `:link-card`. Asides cannot
contain `:tabs`. `:steps` is still an ordered Markdown list or `:step`
children, not both. `:figure` still requires exactly one image.

`@page`, `@roc`, `@render`,
`@component`, handlers, and HTML islands inside a block body are errors.
A colon with a following space (`: definition`) stays Markdown.

`@use "./Callout.rocci"` on `rocdown run` maps each exported `@component` to an
article kind (`Callout` → `:callout`). Unknown `:callout` without `@use` is an
error. Static `rocdown build` and `rocdown check` reject `@use`; custom static
kinds belong in the compiled theme.

| Kind | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `note`, `tip`, `caution`, `danger`, `deprecated` | Labeled asides |
| `details` | Disclosure with required `summary` |
| `steps` / `step` | Ordered procedure; `step` only inside `steps` |
| `figure` | Exactly one image; nested `:img` alt owns accessibility; `caption` and `credit` optional; figure-level `alt` is unknown |
| `definition` | Local term and definition |
| `badge` | Block status label |
| `compatibility` | Table of supported combinations |
| `card-grid` / `link-card` | Related-page cards; `page` is a stable page id |
| `file-tree` | Nested unordered list |
| `tabs` / `tab` | No-JS stacked panels; `kind` is `language`, `platform`, or `tool`; body is `:tab` children only |
| `include` | File or region include |
| `example` | Display sample with optional `test` metadata |
| `api-operation` | Reserved; Rocdown reports `RD2406` (not shipped) |

See [Write documentation components](/docs/guides/docs-components/) for a working
page. Includes, snippet roots, and `rocdown test` are documented in
[Rocdown site](/docs/reference/rocdown-site/).

## Page metadata

````rocdown
@page {
    route: "/guides/rocdown/",
    draft: Bool.false,
    theme: "paper",
    color_scheme: "auto",
    meta: {
        title: "Rocdown",
        description: "Markdown with explicit Roc and Rocci regions",
    },
}
````

| Field | Constraint |
| --- | --- |
| `route` | Absolute string path; no `..`, query, fragment, encoded separator, or NUL |
| `layout` | Statically resolvable Roc value path |
| `draft` | `Bool.true` or `Bool.false` |
| `theme` | Built-in ID, local theme ID, `none`, or CSS file path |
| `color_scheme` | `auto`, `light`, or `dark` |
| `meta` | Roc record; title and description are statically extracted |

## Markdown profile

Rocdown uses CommonMark with GFM tables, strikethrough, task lists, extended
URL autolinks, and footnotes. It adds deterministic heading IDs, stable `rd-*`
classes, language classes on fenced code, wiki links, and page-link resolution.

Raw HTML in Markdown is disabled by default. Use Markdown, a document-root
Rocci tag, or `@render` instead.

## Footnotes

`[^label]` in ordinary Rocdown is a footnote reference. Pair it with a
definition:

````rocdown
The claim is sourced.[^note]

[^note]: Evidence stays with the document.
````

Definitions are collected out of the article flow into a footnotes section.
Standalone lowering and site HTML share the same accessible contract:
`data-footnote-ref`, `aria-label="Footnotes"`, `data-footnote-backref`, and
stable `fn-{name}` / `fnref-{name}` ids. Missing definitions and duplicate
labels are errors at the reference or definition span. This is not an OKF
`sources[].id` citation.

## Links

Sibling preview supports `[[Page]]`, `[[Page|label]]`, Rocdown and Markdown file
paths (including nested relative paths such as `knowledge/decisions/foo.md`),
and same-page heading validation. Absolute routes are checked when a page index
is available. Absolute `*.md` / `*.rocdown` paths suffix-match indexed files
when that match is unique; otherwise they pass through. External schemes such
as `https:` and `mailto:` pass through.

In static site builds, a passing catalog check rewrites validated page and heading links to
the emitted route (`./foo.rocdown` becomes `/foo/`, and `{id}#heading` becomes
`/route/#heading`). Same-page `#heading` stays a fragment. Asset hrefs are
hashed in a later plan pass. Standalone `rocdown run` rewrites sibling stems and
reachable relative document links when `resolve_links` is true, and serves those
linked pages as extra routes.

## Generated values

Every document exports:

```text
rocci_meta    : page metadata record
rocci_content : {} -> Html
rocci_page    : {} -> Html
```

If no GET handler exists for the page route, lowering synthesizes one. A
non-root page also gets a root preview route so `rocdown run` can open it.

The default standalone shell is a single-document reader. When the selected
theme is not `none`, `rocci_page` emits a left `<nav class="rd-toc">` from
heading levels 2 and 3, linking to the same heading IDs used in the article.
H1 is the page title and stays out of the navigator. Empty outlines are
omitted. Theme chrome keeps the article measure and animates navigator jumps
quickly. Below `48rem` the left navigator hides and the same heading IDs appear
in a no-JS `<details class="rd-toc-menu">` control. Print still hides both.
This is not the site outline: site builds keep a right-hand “On this page” rail
inside documentation-site chrome. Site themes that hide a sidebar at the phone
breakpoint must replace it with their own disclosure; rocci.dev uses a header
`<details class="mobile-menu">`.

A custom `@page.layout` replaces that shell and does not receive the
automatic navigator.

## Static documentation site support

Site builds classify each published page as `static`, `hydrate`, or `live` on
top of `:name[params]` article blocks. Blocks such as `:note` and `:tabs` stay
on the Markdown-first path; they do not make a page hydrate or live.

| Kind | What the page may contain | CDN apply | Datastar |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `static` | Markdown, `@page`, `:name[params]` | Widget forest (`DocsComponents`) | No |
| `hydrate` | plus `@component`, `@render`, document-root tags, `@css`, `@roc` | Island Html spliced at build | No |
| `live` | plus `@on` / `@context` / `@init` or `import Datastar` | Same splice plus Datastar.js | Yes |

`@use` stays a site-build error. `@render`, handlers, and HTML islands inside a
`:note` (or other article-block) body are errors. `docs/` is a `static` catalog.
`rocdown run DIR` serves the CDN tree and, for `live` pages, proxies the island
service on the same local origin. `rocdown serve-islands` runs the mutation
service by itself. See [Rocdown site configuration](/docs/reference/rocdown-site/)
for the two-artifact publish, `service_origin`, and `--cdn-only`. Draft pages
are excluded from production builds.

The developer tree spec for owned article and module AST nodes is
`crates/rocci-rocdown/Rocdown.AST.ungram`. It generates Rust types; it does not
generate the scanner or replace this language reference. Markdown remains
`MdNode` until a later tree change. Production names, inspect tags, and sidecar
classification are listed in the
[Rocdown tree appendix](/docs/reference/rocdown-tree/).
